 "stimulus_html": "<figure>\n<figcaption>Venn diagram with two disjoint sets and number of elements in each section.</figcaption>\n<img src=\"exercises/media/4629dfb0ed22b39b.png\" alt=\"A two-set Venn diagram not intersecting one another is given. The first set is labeled A while the second set is labeled B. Set A shows 23. Set B shows 17. Outside the sets, 10 is given. Outside the Venn diagram, it is marked U.\">\n</figure>\n",
 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 494701,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Find <span data-math=\"n(A{\\text{ or }}B)\">n(A{\\text{ or }}B)</span>.",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>To find <i>A</i> or <i>B</i>, find <span data-math=\"A \\cup B\"></span>. The union of two sets includes all the members of the first set and all the members of the second set. Do not list duplicates twice.</p>\n<p>Because the two sets are disjoint, the number of elements in the union of the two sets is the sum of the number of elements in the two sets.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"23 + 17 = 40\"></span></p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "40"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  },
  {
   "id": 494702,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Find <span data-math=\"n (A{\\text{ and }}B)\"> n(A{\\text{ and }}B)</span>.",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>To find <i>A</i> or <i>B</i>, find <span data-math=\"A \\cap B\"></span>. The intersection of two sets includes the elements they have in common. They have no elements in common, so the number of elements in the intersection is zero.</p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "0"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  },
  {
   "id": 494703,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Find <span data-math=\"n({A^\\prime })\">n({A^\\prime })</span>.",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p><span data-math=\"A'\"></span> is the complement of <i>A</i>. The complement of set <i>A</i> is the set of all elements in the universal set <i>U</i> that are <i>not</i> in set <i>A</i>. The number of elements that are not in set <i>A</i>:</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"17 + 10 = 27\"></span></p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "27"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
